From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:25:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(effects): ignore removals for absent unmapped effects

Consume the full MobEffect payload and cancel removal of an effect that
has no Bedrock mapping. Such an effect cannot exist in the translated
entity state because unsupported Add and Update packets still fail.
Keep known-effect removal and its Java packet projection unchanged.

MegaSMP clears IDs 0 through 38 during login. The pinned Bedrock 1.26.60.5
factory registers experimental Freezing as ID 38, while the translated
registry covers IDs 1 through 37. Treating its removal as an attempted
addition disconnects the client before lobby initialization completes.
Do not invent a Java effect mapping for the experimental effect.

An isolated official-client control adds Speed, removes absent ID 38,
then removes Speed. The Speed icon survives the first removal, disappears
after its own removal, and the full 120-second recording remains playable.
The target executable hash and complete packet framing are retained in
private evidence. Packet regressions preserve the known active effect,
consume the payload, project known removal, and reject unsupported adds
and updates.

Discarding other unmapped removals is a robustness policy for absent
state. The native control establishes ID 38 only; mixed invalid-ID native
probes can crash and do not establish behavior for arbitrary integers.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/EntityPackets.java b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/EntityPackets.java
index d6ea7d51c9faca99c6de34ac5d55e1b42b2477ec..f66c7f901f8b44a06e7f1fb19e4051f3c1bf7633 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/EntityPackets.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/EntityPackets.java
@@ -614,7 +614,12 @@ public final class EntityPackets {
             }
 
             final String bedrockIdentifier = BedrockProtocol.MAPPINGS.getBedrockEffects().inverse().get(effectId);
-            if (bedrockIdentifier == null) { // Bedrock client crashes
+            if (bedrockIdentifier == null) {
+                // An unmapped effect cannot exist in the translated entity's retained state.
+                if (event == MobEffectPacketPayload_Event.Remove) {
+                    wrapper.cancel();
+                    return;
+                }
                 throw new IllegalStateException("Unknown bedrock effect: " + effectId);
             }
             final EntityEffect effect = new EntityEffect(bedrockIdentifier, amplifier, duration, showParticles, ambient);
diff --git a/src/test/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/MobEffectPacketTest.java b/src/test/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/protocol/packet/MobEffectPacketTest.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5bec25ba30ceab72985c13db8ad4c06efbbabc34
